<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wu Shifan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1681</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wu Shifan was the grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-sangui">Wu Sangui</a> and the last ruler of the Zhou regime set up during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolt-of-the-three-feudatories">Revolt of the Three Feudatories</a> against the Qing. He succeeded in 1678, retreated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kunming">Kunming</a> as Qing armies advanced, and killed himself when the city fell in 1681, ending the revolt.</p></div>
